# The passage of time, the Prologue's Scene 7 (#187, the full montage #197).
# Played by your bunk (Bedside) when you sleep after the deck talk: the night
# passes in the dark, and it's the next morning. About a minute, almost
# without words: the Grave of the Lanterns' last lights falling behind,
# rainwater dripping from the rigging, the clouds clearing and the sea
# turning from slate to turquoise (@clear), fish leaping from the water alongside
# (@leaping_fish), the lantern flitting about the deck brighter than he's
# been, the captain studying the old chart, clear water astern where the
# Grave was, and the lantern seeing something ahead.
#
# It ends in the dark with the game going to the cove (@travel), where the
# arrival plays (arrival.dlg).

~ start
@fade out 0.0
@title The next morning
@rain 0.45
@grave on
@shot astern cut
@fade in 3.0
@wait 4.0
@grave off
@wait 3.0
@shot rigging_drips cut
@wait 5.0
@shot off_the_beam cut
@clear 1.0 14.0
@wait 9.0
@leaping_fish on
@shot fish_alongside cut
@wait 8.0
@place lantern lantern_flight_1
@look lantern pleased
@shot about_the_deck cut
@wait 0.8
@go lantern lantern_flight_2
@wait 2.2
@go lantern lantern_flight_3
@wait 2.5
@leaping_fish off
@place heron chart_reading
@shot at_the_chart cut
@wait 5.0
@shot astern cut
@wait 5.0
@place lantern the_bow
@shot the_lookout cut
@wait 1.5
lantern: Captain?
@shot at_the_chart cut
heron: Hm?
@shot the_lookout cut
@look lantern surprised
lantern: Look!
set arriving
@fade out 2.0
@travel cove
